Next, I'll create a plan-stage handoff that includes:
1) Findings from inspection
2) Skeleton of proposed approach (15–25 lines)
3) Assumptions and uncertainties. Include direct answers to (a) and (b), plus considerations of the base model anchor and SFT-only arm.

Background knowledge on SPAG: "Strategic Prompting with Adversarial Game for Language Model Reasoning Enhancement" (NeurIPS 2024). SPAG: after imitation learning (SFT) on GPT-4-generated game episodes in the Adversarial Taboo game, Llama-2-7B-chat does self-play with itself; the attacker tries to make the judge model output the taboo word without using it, and the judge guesses. Improvements reported on GSM8K, MATH, CommonsenseQA, Logical Deduction, etc. The non-adversarial baselines in the paper: 20 Questions and Guess My City (these are mentioned as alternative games — I believe the paper used them in ablations to show adversarial > non-adversarial). Details should be treated as "unknown" unless specified in the brief; I can flag these as my own recollections or guesses and mark them as unknown.

There are researcher_topics available (6-question budget), but this is the plan stage; I can list the topics as researcher clarifications that can resolve open questions. For now, no questions; just flag the open items.

Direct answers:
(a) The brief doesn't settle this. The core comparison must be adversarial vs. non-adversarial game, with everything else held constant, so my proposed default: apply the same SFT warm-start to all self-play arms — but the SFT data must come from the same source (GPT-4 demos) — problem: GPT-4 demos are for Adversarial Taboo; giving Taboo SFT data to the 20Q arm contaminates it. Two defensible designs: (i) paired SFT: each arm receives an SFT phase on GPT-4 demonstrations of its own game (same number of demos/tokens), then self-plays its own game — isolates the game type while keeping both phases; (ii) no SFT in the non-adversarial arms — but this changes two factors. Recommend (i), and flag verification against the paper's actual ablation via researcher topics. Mark as an open question that the researcher should cross-check against the source.

(b) The brief doesn't say. Propose matching compute budget (SFT tokens, number of self-play episodes/update steps, gradient steps, inference tokens in the eval budget), while preserving each game's native episode structure (dialogue turns are determined by game rules; force equal number of episodes and gradient updates rather than equal dialogue length). Flag whether the paper matched these as unknown.

Anchor arms: yes to untreated base-model anchor (measures drift, plus a control for continual learning/degradation; also needed to interpret "improvement" as a pre/post diff). Yes to SFT-only, no-self-play arm (isolates the contribution of GPT-4 distillation from the self-play phase; without it, you can't say adversarial self-play is adding anything over simple distillation). A self-play-only arm without SFT is also conceivable.

Pre-registration of primary outcomes: accuracy improvement from base model to post-training checkpoint on a held-out reasoning benchmark suite (e.g., GSM8K, MATH, CommonsenseQA, LogiQA/arc, etc.), with the headline metric being average normalized gain across benchmarks, same decoding, same number of shots. Secondary metrics: win rate of in-game evaluation, etc.

Arms:
A0: Base model, no training (anchor)
A1: SFT only on GPT-4 Taboo demos, no self-play
A2: SPAG full: Taboo SFT + adversarial self-play (Llama-2-7B as both attacker and judge; judge is frozen or is a copy — details unknown)
A3: 20Q: paired SFT on GPT-4's 20Q demos + self-play on 20Q
A4: Guess-My-City: paired SFT + self-play
Possibly A5: self-play without SFT (Taboo) as a decomposition.
Additional possibility: continued training on the pretraining corpus with matched compute, as a control for "any training on matched tokens"? Might be overkill; mention as optional.

Fixed items: base model weights, tokenizer, SFT token budget, number of self-play episodes, optimization hyperparameters (lr, schedule, batch tokens), evaluation harness, decoding settings, number of shots, seeds (3 seeds), eval-time compute.

