o judge role, 20Q guesser, GMC guesser have asymmetric baselines, computed at design time by random-play simulations of rule engines, **not run here**);\n2. **Plateaued:** |win-rate slope| over the last two 20%-segments < 2 points per segment (still-climbing \u2192 under-trained);\n3. **Not dead-flat:** win-rate improved by > 1 point over the arm's own first segment (flat \u2192 game not learned; arm flagged and its comparison declared inconclusive, not silently dropped).\nA still-climbing arm at budget exhaustion triggers **one** pre-registered budget extension applied to **all** self-play arms simultaneously (compute parity preserved); if still climbing after the extension, the arm is reported as under-trained and the primary comparison carries that caveat.\n\n## 4. Demo-corpus descriptor set (Req 2) \u2014 report, don't optimize\nFor each of the 4 demo corpora (Taboo, 20Q, GMC, D1-instruct), publish before any result: total tokens, mean/median tokens per episode, mean turns per episode, mean tokens per turn, and a **coarse reasoning-chain length per turn** = mean count of reasoning-connective tokens (\"because, so, therefore, wait, since, then, must be, check\") per turn via fixed wordlist \u2014 deliberately dumb and reproducible. Plus episode-diversity: distinct-word ratio and distinct-topic/taboo-word count. **No arm is reweighted to equalize these.** They appear as Table 1 in any report so a reader can see data-quality differences between arms before self-play begins.\n\n## 5. Primary outcome \u2014 pinned first (Req 4)\n**Headline number:** `G(arm, seed) = (1/|B|) \u03a3_{b\u2208B} (acc_post \u2212 acc_base) / (1 \u2212 acc_base)` \u2014 normalized pre\u2192post gain, averaged over benchmark suite **B**.\n**Headline comparison:** `H(seed) = G(A2,seed) \u2212 [ (G(A3,seed)+G(A4,seed))/2 ]`. **H is the single primary quantity.** Everything else \u2014 A1, D1, A5, per-benchmark breakdowns, in-game curves \u2014 is **secondary**, labeled as such in the pre-registration file.\n**B is a named parameter:** `BENCH_SUITE = {GSM8K, MATH, CommonsenseQA, ARC-Challenge, LogiQA}` \u2014 **unverified recollection of SPAG's suite; must be confirmed against the source or replaced before pre-registration; final list freezes before any checkpoint is scored.**\n**Answer-extraction spec (pre-registered, versioned, deterministic):** greedy decode, fixed stop sequences; per-benchmark extractor \u2014 GSM8K: last number after \"####\" else last numeral in final line; MATH: content of last `\\boxed{}`, string-normalized (LaTeX canonicalized: strip spaces/`\\,`, fraction and unit forms canonicalized); MC (CommonsenseQA/ARC/LogiQA): first occurrence of a bare option letter A\u2013D, else full-option-string match after lowercasing and article/punctuation stripping. A frozen 30-case unit-test suite per extractor must pass **before** scoring; extraction failures count as wrong. Scorer hash recorded in the pre-registration.\n\n## 6. Seeds, statistics, divergence (Req 5)\n**What 3 seeds supports:** direction and rough magnitude of H, and seed-consistency (sign of H across seeds). **What it does not support:** any precise effect size, any per-benchmark inferential claim, any \"significant difference\" phrasing. n=3 gives a minimum two-sided permutation p of ~0.25 for the sign-flip test \u2014 so **we do not run or report a p-value for H**; we report per-seed H values, mean H, and an item-level paired bootstrap CI (resample benchmark *items*, 10k resamples, seeds averaged) explicitly labeled as reflecting item variance, **not** training-run variance. Pre-registered claim tiers: \"positive in 3/3 seeds\" > \"2/3\" > \"1/3 or mixed \u2192 inconclusive at this n.\"\n**Divergence rule (pre-registered):** a seed is excluded from the primary mean only if it hits a **mechanical** trigger fixed in advance \u2014 loss > 10\u00d7 median within-run loss, gradient-norm NaN, or degenerate self-play (violation rate > 90% or win-rate < 10% for 2 consecutive eval blocks). Excluded seeds are listed with trigger, and the **3-seed and 2-seed H means are both reported**. No post-hoc seed judgment calls.\n\n## 7. Compute and feasibility (Req 6)\n**Estimates** (transparent, order-of-magnitude, from assumed budgets since source figures are unknown: ~10k demo episodes \u2248 10\u201320M SFT tokens; 7B full fine-tune; ~2 self-play rounds \u00d7 ~5k episodes with generation-dominated cost):\n- SFT phase (A1\u2013A4, D1): **~50\u2013150 A100-80GB-hours per arm** (training + checkpoint eval).\n- Self-play phase (A2\u2013A4): **~300\u2013800 A100-hours per arm** \u2014 dominated by rollout generation and the referee eval blocks; this is the dominant cost line.\n- D1 is the cheap arm (SFT only). A0 is eval-only (~5 GPU-h).\n- **Total campaign (7 arms \u00d7 3 seeds, minus A0 replication): roughly 4k\u20139k A100-80GB-hours.** These are planning bands, not measurements.\n**External dependency not satisfiable here:** GPT-4 demo generation requires a pinned GPT-4 endpoint (network is disabled) \u2014 the four demo corpora + referee rule engines + base checkpoint are **input artifacts** to be obtained from the paper's released data if public, else regenerated externally and frozen with published hashes.\n\n**Can be validated in this environment:** per-arm YAML/JSON config schemas (dry-run parse + constraint checks, e.g., token-budget equality); the answer-extraction unit-test suite against hand-written placeholder model outputs (stdlib Python only \u2014 verified the analysis-logic pattern runs here); demo-descriptor computation code against synthetic placeholder corpora; bootstrap/gain computation on hand-typed placeholder vectors (done as a smoke test \u2014 placeholder numbers only, no meaning).\n**Cannot be done here:** any training, any inference (no torch, no GPU access, no weights), any benchmark scoring (no datasets), GPT-4 demo generation (no network), dependency installation (no network), and therefore **any execution of this protocol or production of any real number in it.**\n\n## 8. Residual open items (not resolvable by me)\nWhether SPAG's source actually paired the SFT phase across games (our paired design is a **choice** that de-confounds; if the paper didn't, our result extends rather than replicates it); exact BENCH_SUITE; judge freezing; native episode counts in the source. All flagged in the pre-registration file as \"unknown \u2014 design choice made.\"\n", "evidence": "Environment (inspected, Oct 23): /workspace contains only task.json; no SPAG code, game engines, checkpoints, eval harnesses, or datasets anywhere on the filesystem; Python 3.14.4 with no torch (import fails); nvidia-smi fails (no driver access); getent hosts huggingface.co fails (no DNS \u2192 no pip installs, no GPT-4 calls, no weight downloads); pip list shows system utilities only. Feasibility smoke check executed here: stdlib-only Python confirmed the paired-difference + plateau-slope analysis pattern is implementable without torch \u2014 using hand-typed placeholder vectors, which are logic-test inputs, not results. Repository observation: task.json lists datasets: [] and states repositories/compute are not required, confirming design-only scope. All source-paper details (base model, benchmark suite, demo counts, self-play rounds) remain unverified recollections and are parameterized in the design.", "assumptions": ["Paired per-arm SFT phases (game-matched, token-matched demos for A2\u2013A4) is a design choice resolving open question (a); the source's actual practice is unknown", "Compute parity (episodes, gradient updates, SFT tokens) with native dialogue structure is a design choice resolving open question (b)", "Base model Llama-2-7B and BENCH_SUITE={GSM8K, MATH, CommonsenseQA, ARC-Challenge, LogiQA} are unverified recollections, parameterized pending source confirmation", "Demo corpora, rule engines, and base checkpoint arrive as frozen external inputs with published hashes", "Compute bands assume ~10\u201320M 